WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.297
Long form is often the more flexible analytical shape.

00:00:03.297 --> 00:00:08.272
If categories change frequently, new values simply appear in rows.

00:00:08.272 --> 00:00:15.502
Long form also works naturally with trend charts, filtering, grouping, and many modeling workflows.

00:00:15.502 --> 00:00:20.042
It avoids changing the schema every time a new category appears.

00:00:20.042 --> 00:00:26.417
Long and wide are not labels for good and bad design; they are shapes suited to different tasks.

00:00:26.417 --> 00:00:31.927
Long data is often easier for grouping, plotting, and scalable storage.

00:00:31.927 --> 00:00:37.687
Wide data is often convenient for human-readable reports or some modeling interfaces.

00:00:37.687 --> 00:00:40.320
Choose the shape required by the next step.
